.TH TAZTERM 1 "2026-09-25" "tazterm 0.9.1" "SliTaz"
.SH NAME
tazterm \- light GTK3/VTE terminal with split panes, AI friendly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tazterm
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fB\-e\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.br
.B tazterm help
.br
.B tazterm ctl
\fBls\fR | \fBread\fR | \fBblocks\fR | \fBwait\fR | \fBevents\fR | \fBnotify\fR | \fBguide\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
TazTerm is the SliTaz terminal: split panes in one window, a status
line per pane, command blocks for bash, safe paste, and a read-only
control socket so AI agents (claude, opencode, navette) can see the
user's panes instead of asking for copy and paste.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-working\-directory =\fIDIR\fR
Start the shell in \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shell =\fISHELL\fR
Shell to run. Default: \fBshell\fR in the config; \fBauto\fR (the
default) means bash when installed, else /bin/sh.
.TP
.BR \-e " " \fICOMMAND\fR " [" \fIARGS\fR ...]
Run \fICOMMAND\fR instead of a shell; everything after \fB\-e\fR belongs
to it. A single argument with spaces is parsed as a command line.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-title " " \fITITLE\fR
Window title.
.TP
.BR \-geometry " " \fICOLS\fRx\fIROWS\fR[+\fIX\fR+\fIY\fR]
Terminal size in characters, optional position.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-hold
Keep the \fB\-e\fR pane open after the command ends, with its exit code.
.TP
.BR \-\-class =\fICLASS\fR ", " \-\-name =\fINAME\fR
WM_CLASS for the window manager.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-version
Print the version (no display needed).
.PP
Single-dash long options (\fB\-geometry\fR, \fB\-title\fR, \fB\-hold\fR)
follow xterm, as used by the SliTaz \fBterminal\fR wrapper.
.SH KEYS
Defaults below; every shortcut can be changed in [keys].
\fBF1\fR (or \fBtazterm help\fR in a pane) lists the ones in use.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C / V / Q
Copy, paste, quit (asks when a program still runs).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E / O / W
Split side by side, split stacked, close pane.
.TP
.B Alt+Arrows
Move to the neighbor pane.
.TP
.B Alt+Shift+Arrows
Move the active pane's border.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Z / B
Zoom the active pane (again to restore), equalize pane sizes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Up / Down
Jump to the previous / next prompt (bash panes).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Find in the scrollback.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A / T / X
Open an agent split, send the selection to the agent, send the last
command (or the last lines) to the agent. Nothing is submitted: the
user adds a question and presses Enter.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Copy the scrollback to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+click
Open a URL with $BROWSER, or \fIfile\fR:\fIline\fR in a terminal editor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Plus / Minus / 0, F11
Zoom, fullscreen.
.SH ALERTS
A bell (BEL) from a pane you are not in, or a command of at least
\fBnotify_after\fR seconds (30, bash panes) that ends out of sight,
outlines the pane in orange and sets the window urgency hint when it
is not focused.
.SH PASTE
Control characters are stripped. A multi-line paste into a shell
without bracketed paste (busybox ash), where each line would run at
once, asks for confirmation first.
.SH COMMAND BLOCKS
bash panes start with \fB\-\-rcfile\fR ~/.config/tazterm/bash-integration.sh,
which sources ~/.bashrc and marks each prompt. tazterm then knows every
command, its output, exit code and duration. busybox ash has no prompt
hook: no blocks there.
.SH TAZTERM CTL
Every pane exports TAZTERM_SOCKET, TAZTERM_PANE and TERM_PROGRAM=tazterm.
The socket is read-only: a program may read panes, never type into them.
.TP
.B ls
Panes: id, role, state, activity (busy, idle, bell, exited), process,
cwd, title.
.TP
.BR read " [" \-p " " \fIID\fR "] [" \-n " " \fIN\fR " | " \-a " | " \-l ]
Last lines of a pane; \fB\-l\fR: its last command block. Without \fB\-p\fR:
the pane the user came from.
.TP
.BR blocks " [" \-p " " \fIID\fR "] [" \-n " " \fIN\fR ]
Recent commands with exit code and duration.
.TP
.BR wait " [" \-p " " \fIID\fR "] [" \-t " " \fISECS\fR ]
Wait for the next command of a pane to end, print it, exit with its
status.
.TP
.BR wait " \-\-idle [" \-p " " \fIID\fR "] [" \-s " " \fISECS\fR "] [" \-t " " \fISECS\fR ]
Wait until a pane has been quiet \fB\-s\fR seconds (5), rings the bell
or exits; print \fBidle\fR \fIN\fRs, \fBbell\fR or \fBexited\fR \fIN\fR.
Any pane: an agent following another agent's turn.
.TP
.BR events
Stream pane events, one line each, until interrupted:
\fBblock\fR \fIPANE EXIT SECS COMMAND\fR, \fBbell\fR \fIPANE\fR,
\fBnotify\fR \fIPANE TEXT\fR, \fBopen\fR, \fBexit\fR \fIPANE N\fR,
\fBclose\fR.
.TP
.BR notify " [" \fITEXT\fR ]
Outline the caller's pane in orange and set the window urgency hint.
.TP
.B guide
How an AI agent should use tazterm (markdown).
.PP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR on ls, read, blocks, wait and events: JSON output.
.PP
Keys, tokens and passwords are masked as [REDACTED] unless
\fBredact=false\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tazterm/tazterm.conf
Configuration (created with every key and comments): font, shell,
theme (slitaz, tango, solarized-dark, solarized-light, vte), cursor
shape, status line, alerts, agent. Every shortcut can be changed in
[keys] (action=Ctrl+Shift+E, several separated by spaces, empty to
leave the key to the application).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tazterm/shell-integration.sh, bash-integration.sh
Shell hooks, managed by tazterm.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tazterm/PID.sock
Control socket (else ~/.cache/tazterm/), directory 0700.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
TAZTERM_DEBUG=1 (logs on stderr), TAZTERM_SHELL, TAZTERM_AGENT_CMD.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR terminal (1),
.BR vte (3)
